Spectrum Virtualize asks for a primary key server. The primary key server represents only the KeySecure server that is used for key create and rekey operations. Therefore, any of the clustered key servers can be selected as the primary.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":270.0998639999998,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":151.200168,"r":547.4089680000012,"t":315.3122879999999},"charspan":[0,314],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/29","text":"Although Gemalto SafeNet KeySecure uses an active-active clustered model, IBM Spectrum Virtualize asks for a primary key server. The primary key server represents only the KeySecure server that is used for key create and rekey operations. Therefore, any of the clustered key servers can be selected as the primary."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Selecting a primary key server is beneficial for load balancing. Any four key servers can be used to retrieve the master key.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":241.12024799999983,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":151.200168,"r":547.5762960000002,"t":262.33305599999983},"charspan":[0,125],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"Selecting a primary key server is beneficial for load balancing. Any four key servers can be used to retrieve the master key."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"Chapter 12. Encryption 637","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":27.938279999999963,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":423.6,"r":547.2169440000001,"t":37.15128000000004},"charspan":[0,26],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"Chapter 12. Encryption 637"}],"version":"1.10.0"}